// PersonState.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Local and/or Nested types and functions,
//       Target-Set Syntax, Declaration-Reference Syntax
//
// FoLang has no Java/C++/C#-style physical nesting. A declaration that exists
// only for particular targets stays an ordinary package declaration and is
// restricted with @co.dap.local.
//
// Supported annotated kinds: class, struct, enum, module, and named functions.
// Every target must resolve to exactly one class, struct, enum, module, or
// function overload, and must live in the same exact folder-derived package —
// parent and subpackages are different packages.
//
// Scalar form for one target:
//
//     @co.dap.local(for=Person)
//
// List form for several, which is a closed set: visibility is the union of the
// listed target scopes and is neither inherited nor transitive. Duplicate or
// empty target lists are compiler errors, and repeated @co.dap.local
// annotations do not accumulate — use one annotation with the full list.

@co.dap.local(
    for=[
        Person,
        PersonStoreImpl
    ]
)
_ co.lang.enum = {
    Active,
    Inactive,
    Pending
}

// The local declaration is visible while compiling its targets, but it never
// becomes a nested name such as Person.PersonState, and ordinary visibility
// annotations cannot widen it beyond the listed target set.
